commit 15e259feb08891dfa13956e63d930a53940aea7c

C03: a backup or copy to a pendrive first reads which removable drives are connected, and says truthfully when there is none (USB1823)

New read-only operation storage.removable.list: the removable drives ready right now through DriveInfo (letter, label, format, free and total GiB); nothing is copied. The mind reads «hacé un backup / copiá / guardá … a un pendrive / usb / disco externo» and «qué pendrives hay conectados» as that read (never formatting, deleting or ejecting), and the composer says that no pendrive or USB drive is connected, that nothing was copied and that the person can plug one in and ask again, or names the drives with their free space; numbers and invented copies are checked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


